Model 'General Piece Dynamics' (GPD) posits that the mechanism of physics itself stems from a universal law: all entities ('pieces') must operate a 'piece computer' that computes and calculates the passage of a piece along its worldline. This 'piece computer' is essential for performing the physics of the model, especially given the complexity required for describing optimized emergent systems. The fundamental law is stated as 'physics manifests by emerging as piece computers,' and all contents of blob follow these same physical laws. Thus, every piece possesses a piece computer, one per defining world. The piece computer requires a 2³-dimensional ontology to describe any object/concept of interest to an operator (or piece), whereas things outside this interest are 'not of interest.' Blob is defined as the universal piece computer, representing the singular network of all world piece computers. The model takes General Relativity (GR) to its logical extreme to unify GR with Quantum Field Theory (QFT). The structure involves a top-level 'blob' dimension where each 'blob piece' has its own 2³ hierarchical space that nests, segmenting BLOB into a singular/plural duality: the top is a singular, continuous manifold (Blob), while descending levels differentiate into more distinct pieces at the bottom ('plural'). GR describes the top-level singular manifold, while quantum physics applies to lower-level pieces, each as a unique fundamental quantum, with the top-level manifold representing the zero-order quantization where blob is the fundamental quantum. Quanta pieces exist as components of a wavefunction defining the piecespace of a blob piece’s piece computer in a given world.

